// 4212265) is a general DEM-contact/parallel-decomposition problem, independent of any fluid
// coupling -- no water, no LBM fields, no hydrodynamic coupling at all, just cuboids dropped under
// gravity into a solid-walled box (walls on ALL 6 sides -- periodicity <0,0,0>), released in
// staggered waves (startInactive + settlingSteps, the same mechanism already used in production
// FloatingBoxes) so the pile builds up gradually along Z (the domain's tall/main-height axis; gravity
// is hardcoded to Z in this codebase's AddExternalForces, see DropTest.cpp's own header comment for
// why Z specifically, not X/Y).
//
// SCALE (per explicit request): 1000 cuboids total, released 10 at a time (one per spawn column)
// every 1500 timesteps -- 100 waves x 10 columns, settlingSteps 0,1500,...,148500 -- then the run
// continues 10000 more steps after the last wave lands/settles (timesteps=158500). 1500 steps (not
// the originally-planned 500) because 500 deterministically hit [RELEASE-OVERLAP] -- see the
// FloatingBoxes block below for the full explanation and the exact 10-column layout.
//
// DOMAIN: <32, 30, 180>, cellsPerBlock <16, 10, 30> -> numBlocks (2, 3, 6) = 36 blocks/processes
